ring|null)[], ...} $args' ),","+\t\t\t),","+\t\t\t'a var hash is left alone'                    => array(","+\t\t\t\t'<?php","+\t\t\t\tclass WP_Tests_Hash {","+\t\t\t\t\t/**","+\t\t\t\t\t * @var array {","+\t\t\t\t\t *     @type string $name Name.","+\t\t\t\t\t * }","+\t\t\t\t\t */","+\t\t\t\t\tpublic $args = array();","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\t',","+\t\t\t\tarray(),","+\t\t\t),","+\t\t\t'a hook docblock on a statement is translated' => array(","+\t\t\t\t'<?php","+\t\t\t\t/**","+\t\t\t\t * Filters the arguments.","+\t\t\t\t *","+\t\t\t\t * @param array $args {","+\t\t\t\t *     @type string $name Name.","+\t\t\t\t * }","+\t\t\t\t */","+\t\t\t\t$args = apply_filters( \"wp_tests\", $args );","+\t\t\t\t',","+\t\t\t\tarray( '@phpstan-param array{name?: string, ...} $args' ),","+\t\t\t),","+\t\t\t'a docblock without a hash is left alone'     => array(","+\t\t\t\tself::fn(","+\t\t\t\t\t'","+\t\t\t\t\t * @param array $args Arguments. See the @type tags elsewhere.","+\t\t\t\t\t * @return array","+\t\t\t\t\t'","+\t\t\t\t),","+\t\t\t\tarray(),","+\t\t\t),","+\t\t);","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Tests that the rewritten docblock keeps everything it had, and gains its tags","+\t * before the closing marker.","+\t */","+\tpublic function test_rewritten_docblock_keeps_the_original_text(): void {","+\t\t$code = self::fn(","+\t\t\t'","+\t\t\t * Does a thing.","+\t\t\t *","+\t\t\t * @since 1.0.0","+\t\t\t *","+\t\t\t * @param array $args {","+\t\t\t *     @type string $name Name.","+\t\t\t * }","+\t\t\t * @return void","+\t\t\t'","+\t\t);","+","+\t\t$docblocks = self::docblocks_after_visiting( $code );","+","+\t\t$this->assertCount( 1, $docblocks );","+\t\t$this->assertStringContainsString( \"Does a thing.\\n\", $docblocks[0] );","+\t\t$this->assertStringContainsString( \"@since 1.0.0\\n\", $docblocks[0] );","+\t\t$this->assertStringContainsString( \"@return void\\n\", $docblocks[0] );","+\t\t$this->assertStringEndsWith( \" * @phpstan-param array{name?: string, ...} \\$args\\n */\", $docblocks[0] );","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Wraps a docblock body in a function declaration.","+\t *","+\t * @param string $body      Docblock lines, each starting with ` * `.","+\t * @param string $signature Parameter list.","+\t * @return string","+\t */","+\tprivate static function fn( string $body, string $signature = '( $args )' ): string {","+\t\treturn \"<?php\\n/**\" . rtrim( $body ) . \"\\n */\\nfunction wp_tests_fn\" . $signature . \" {}\\n\";","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Returns the `@phpstan-*` lines the docblocks in a snippet gain from the visitor.","+\t *","+\t * Each line present beforehand is removed only once, rather than every line equal to it,","+\t * so that a tag the visitor writes a second time is still returned.","+\t *","+\t * @param string $code PHP source.","+\t * @return list<string>","+\t */","+\tprivate static function derived_tags( string $code ): array {","+\t\t$before = self::phpstan_lines( self::docblocks( $code, false ) );","+\t\t$after  = self::phpstan_lines( self::docblocks_after_visiting( $code ) );","+","+\t\tforeach ( $before as $line ) {","+\t\t\t$key = array_search( $line, $after, true );","+\t\t\tif ( false !== $key ) {","+\t\t\t\tunset( $after[ $key ] );","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+","+\t\treturn array_values( $after );","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Returns the docblocks in a snippet after the visitor has run.","+\t *","+\t * @param string $code PHP source.","+\t * @return list<string>","+\t */","+\tprivate static function docblocks_after_visiting( string $code ): array {","+\t\treturn self::docblocks( $code, true );","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Returns the text of every docblock in a snippet.","+\t *","+\t * @param string $code  PHP source.","+\t * @param bool   $visit Whether to run the visitor first.","+\t * @return list<string>","+\t */","+\tprivate static function docblocks( string $code, bool $visit ): array {","+\t\t$stmts = ( new ParserFactory() )->createForHostVersion()->parse( $code );","+\t\tself::assertNotNull( $stmts );","+","+\t\t$collector = new class() extends NodeVisitorAbstract {","+\t\t\t/**","+\t\t\t * @var list<string>","+\t\t\t */","+\t\t\tpublic array $docblocks = array();","+","+\t\t\tpublic function enterNode( Node $node ): ?Node {","+\t\t\t\t$doc = $node->getDocComment();","+\t\t\t\tif ( null !== $doc ) {","+\t\t\t\t\t$this->docblocks[] = $doc->getText();","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\treturn null;","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t};","+","+\t\t$traverser = new NodeTraverser();","+\t\tif ( $visit ) {","+\t\t\t$traverser->addVisitor( new HashNotationVisitor() );","+\t\t}","+\t\t$traverser->addVisitor( $collector );","+\t\t$traverser->traverse( $stmts );","+","+\t\treturn $collector->docblocks;","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Extracts the `@phpstan-*` tag lines from docblocks, without their furniture.","+\t *","+\t * @param list<string> $docblocks Docblock texts.","+\t * @return list<string>","+\t */","+\tprivate static function phpstan_lines( array $docblocks ): array {","+\t\t$lines = array();","+\t\tforeach ( $docblocks as $docblock ) {","+\t\t\tif ( preg_match_all( '#^\\s*\\*\\s*(@phpstan-\\S+ .*)$#m', $docblock, $matches ) > 0 ) {","+\t\t\t\tforeach ( $matches[1] as $line ) {","+\t\t\t\t\t$lines[] = rtrim( $line );","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t\treturn $lines;","+\t}","+}"],"additions":558,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/phpstan/Tests/HookDocBlockTest.php","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@","+<?php","+/**","+ * Tests for HookDocBlock.","+ *","+ * @package WordPress","+ */","+","+declare(strict_types=1);","+","+namespace WordPress\\PHPStan\\Tests;","+","+use PhpParser\\Node\\Expr\\FuncCall;","+use PhpParser\\NodeFinder;","+use PhpParser\\ParserFactory;","+use PHPStan\\Testing\\PHPStanTestCase;","+use WordPress\\PHPStan\\HookDocBlock;","+","+/**","+ * Checks the helpers the rules share.","+ *","+ * Resolving documentation for a call is covered end to end by the rule tests and","+ * the return type extension test.","+ */","+final class HookDocBlockTest extends PHPStanTestCase {","+","+\t/**","+\t * Returns the configuration registering the services under test.","+\t *","+\t * @return list<string>","+\t */","+\tpublic static function getAdditionalConfigFiles(): array {","+\t\treturn array( __DIR__ . '/tests.neon' );","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * @dataProvider data_hook_names","+\t *","+\t * @param string $call         Hook call expression.","+\t * @param bool   $identifiable Whether the hook name carries literal text.","+\t * @param string $display      How the name is rendered in messages.","+\t */","+\tpublic function test_hook_names( string $call, bool $identifiable, string $display ): void {","+\t\t$node = self::call( $call );","+","+\t\t$this->assertSame( $identifiable, HookDocBlock::hasIdentifiableHookName( $node ) );","+\t\t$this->assertSame( $display, HookDocBlock::getHookNameDisplay( $node ) );","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * @return array<string, array{string, bool, string}>","+\t */","+\tpublic function data_hook_names(): array {","+\t\treturn array(","+\t\t\t'literal'                       => array( \"apply_filters( 'the_content', \\$c )\", true, 'the_content' ),","+\t\t\t'interpolated with literal'     => array( 'apply_filters( \"pre_option_{$option}\", $v )', true, 'pre_option_{$option}' ),","+\t\t\t'interpolated without literal'  => array( 'apply_filters( \"{$hook}\", $v )', false, '{$hook}' ),","+\t\t\t'interpolated separators only'  => array( 'apply_filters( \"{$taxonomy}_{$field}\", $v )', true, '{$taxonomy}_{$field}' ),","+\t\t\t'interpolated property fetch'   => array( 'apply_filters( \"manage_{$this->screen->id}_columns\", $v )', true, 'manage_{...}_columns' ),","+\t\t\t'concatenated with literal'     => array( \"apply_filters( 'prefix_' . \\$name, \\$v )\", true, 'prefix_$name' ),","+\t\t\t'concatenated variables'        => array( 'apply_filters( $a . $b, $v )', false, '$a$b' ),","+\t\t\t'variable'                      => array( 'apply_filters( $hook_name, $v )', false, '$hook_name' ),","+\t\t\t'other expression'              => array( 'apply_filters( wp_tests_name(), $v )', false, '...' ),","+\t\t\t'no arguments'                  => array( 'apply_filters()', false, '' ),","+\t\t);","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Tests that a filter resolving to a docblock without parameters is flagged,","+\t * and an action is not.","+\t */","+\tpublic function test_is_filter_missing_param_docs(): void {","+\t\t$without = array(","+\t\t\t'kind'       => 'inline',","+\t\t\t'resolved'   => null,","+\t\t\t'paramCount' => 0,","+\t\t\t'problem'    => null,","+\t\t);","+\t\t$with    = array_merge( $without, array( 'paramCount' => 1 ) );","+\t\t$unknown = array_merge( $without, array( 'paramCount' => null ) );","+","+\t\t$this->assertTrue( HookDocBlock::isFilterMissingParamDocs( self::call( \"apply_filters( 'a', \\$v )\" ), $without ) );","+\t\t$this->assertTrue( HookDocBlock::isFilterMissingParamDocs( self::call( \"apply_filters_ref_array( 'a', \\$v )\" ), $without ) );","+\t\t$this->assertTrue( HookDocBlock::isFilterMissingParamDocs( self::call( \"apply_filters_deprecated( 'a', \\$v, '1.0' )\" ), $without ) );","+\t\t$this->assertFalse( HookDocBlock::isFilterMissingParamDocs( self::call( \"do_action( 'a', \\$v )\" ), $without ) );","+\t\t$this->assertFalse( HookDocBlock::isFilterMissingParamDocs( self::call( \"apply_filters( 'a', \\$v )\" ), $with ) );","+\t\t$this->assertFalse( HookDocBlock::isFilterMissingParamDocs( self::call( \"apply_filters( 'a', \\$v )\" ), $unknown ) );","+\t}","+","+\t/**","+\t * Parses a hook call expression.","+\t *","+\t * @param string $call PHP expression.","+\t * @return FuncCall","+\t */","+\tprivate static function call( string $call ): FuncCall {","+\t\t$stmts = ( new ParserFactory() )->createForHostVersion()->parse( '<?php ' . $call . ';' );","+\t\tself::assertNotNull( $stmts );","+","+\t\t$calls = ( new NodeFinder() )->findInstanceOf( $stmts, FuncCall::class );","+\t\tself::assertNotEmpty( $calls );","+","+\t\treturn $calls[0];","+\t}","+}"],"additions":104,"deletions":0,"t